SDL3 WebGPU GPU backend for the Tessera web binding.

Derived from SDL PR #16020 "GPU: Experimental WebGPU SDLGPU Backend"
by @TheeStickmahn (https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/pull/16020,
head fc33cbae21211b24aa5a8525fbb3c5004ead2a8d, zlib license),
rebased onto the vendored SDL 3.4.12 in third_party/SDL:
  - CMakeLists.txt / SDL_gpu.h / dynapi hunks re-anchored for 3.4.12
  - XR session/swapchain driver stubs removed (no XR vtable in 3.4.12)
  - reflection honors a "//!nofilter" marker on WGSL texture/sampler
    declarations (unfilterable-float + non-filtering layout entries, needed
    for sampling depth textures)
  - pushed-uniform tracking reset moved from BindVertexBuffers to
    BindGraphicsPipeline, and re-pushing a slot updates the queued bind in
    place (SDLGPU allows push-then-bind-vertex-buffers order)
  - vertex arrayStride taken from the declared vertex_buffer_descriptions
    pitch instead of being guessed from attribute sizes/offsets

Apply with tools/web/patch_sdl.sh — never patch third_party/SDL in place.

